 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "34:1-6 not glossed: Al-Muyassar limits the term to the punishment of disbelieving nations, As-Sa'di makes it the term of every nation and person. An hourglass for «أجل». Light for «فمن اتقى وأصلح». The Fire (36): no motif, nothing literal. First-person «رسلي… كتابي… سخطي» not used. STAGING v4: c1 (34: every nation has its term): people walk into a town at dusk with an hourglass plate; the camera stays on them (no pan pushes them off the frame) and nothing happens to them, since Al-Muyassar makes the term the punishment of denying nations and As-Sa'di the term of every nation and person: only what both share (a nation, a term) is drawn. c2 (35-36): the messengers (35:5) are not drawn and nobody acts inside the conditional clause; a book plate stands for the verses related (35:7). The camera comes to the believers on 35:8; on 35:13-18 (no fear on them, nor grief) a light plate and a soft sparkle; they do not pray under the plate. On 36:1 the camera moves to the three deniers: they shake their heads (they denied) and turn away (they were arrogant). For 36:6-11 the camera goes wide over the town and a seal plate stands on 36:7; nothing falls on the people, and the Fire is not pictured (no fire motif, no darkness)."
